    "intro": "The cost to visit Machu Picchu in 2026 can range between $60 and $250 USD per person, depending on whether you travel on your own or choose an organized tour from Cusco. See tour to Machu Picchu available",
    "content_html": "\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-large is-resized\"><img alt=\"experiences-machu-picchu-travel-tips-peru-cusco\" class=\"wp-image-1063\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"576\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" src=\"https://www.gtperutravel.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/experiencias-machu-picchu-travel-tips-peru-cusco-1024x576.jpg\" srcset=\"https://www.gtperutravel.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/experiencias-machu-picchu-travel-tips-peru-cusco-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://www.gtperutravel.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/experiencias-machu-picchu-travel-tips-peru-cusco-300x169.jpg 300w, https://www.gtperutravel.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/experiencias-machu-picchu-travel-tips-peru-cusco-768x432.jpg 768w, https://www.gtperutravel.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/experiencias-machu-picchu-travel-tips-peru-cusco.jpg 1200w\" style=\"width:459px;height:auto\" width=\"1024\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">experiences-machu-picchu-travel-tips-peru-cusco</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"de-qu-e-depende-el-precio\"> What does the price depend on?</h2>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The total cost is not just the entrance fee. It includes several factors:</p>\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li> Entrance to Machu Picchu</li>\n<li> Transportation (train or alternative route)</li>\n<li> Upload bus (optional)</li>\n<li> Tour guide (recommended)</li>\n<li> Accommodation (if you do 2 days)</li>\n</ul>\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"precios-aproximados-2026\"> Approximate prices (2026)</h2>\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"entrada-a-machu-picchu\"> Entrance to Machu Picchu</h3>\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Foreigner: <strong>$40 – $60 USD</strong></li>\n<li>Andean Community: <strong>$25 – $40 USD</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"tren-ida-y-vuelta\"> Train (round trip)</h3>\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Economical: <strong>$120 – $160 USD</strong></li>\n<li>Tourist: <strong>$180 – $250 USD</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"bus-aguas-calientes-machu-picchu\"> Bus Aguas Calientes – Machu Picchu</h3>\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Round trip: <strong>$24 USD</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"gu-ia-tur-istico\"> Tour guide</h3>\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Shared: <strong>$10 – $20 USD</strong></li>\n<li>Private: <strong>$40 – $80 USD</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"tour-completo-recomendado\"> Complete tour (recommended)</h3>\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Full Day from Cusco: <strong>$250 – $350 USD</strong></li>\n<li>2 days / 1 night: <strong>$300 – $500 USD</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ir-por-cuenta-propia-o-con-tour\"> Go on your own or with a tour?</h2>\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"por-cuenta-propia\"> On your own</h3>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> More flexible<br/> It can be cheaper<br/> Requires planning<br/> Risk of errors (tickets, schedules)</p>\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"con-tour-organizado\"> With organized tour</h3>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> All included<br/> No stress<br/> Better use of time<br/> Professional guide</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> <strong>Recommended if it's your first time</strong></p>\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"consejo-clave\"> Key tip</h2>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Book in advance, especially in high season (May – September).<br/>Tickets to Machu Picchu sell out quickly.</p>\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recomendaci-on\"> Recommendation</h2>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you want to avoid complications and ensure your income, it is best to opt for an organized tour from Cusco.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> <strong>See available tours:</strong><br/> <a href=\"https://www.gtperutravel.com/tour/template-tour.php?tour=machupicchu&amp;lang=es\">Machu Picchu Full Day</a><br/> <a href=\"https://www.gtperutravel.com/paquete/template-paquete.php?paquete=vallesagrado-machupicchu&amp;lang=es\">Machu Picchu 2 days</a></p>\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"preguntas-relacionadas\"> Related questions</h2>\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://www.gtperutravel.com/blog/mejor-hora-para-visitar-machu-picchu-evita-multitudes-y-disfruta-mejores-vistas/\">What is the best time to visit Machu Picchu?</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.gtperutravel.com/blog/como-llegar-a-machu-picchu-desde-cusco/\">How to get to Machu Picchu from Cusco?</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.gtperutravel.com/blog/cuantos-dias-necesito-para-visitar-cusco-y-machu-picchu/\">How many days do I need to visit Cusco?</a></li>\n</ul>\n",
